    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Program-Director-Instructor---Energy-Management-Landman-Program_JR100650": {
      "title": "Program Director/Instructor – Energy Management/Landman Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: The Davis School of Business at Colorado Mesa University is seeking candidates for the Program Director/Instructor – Energy Management/Landman Program. Candidates may come from diverse backgrounds, with a range of experiences, achievements, and leadership roles, either within or outside academia. Candidates should have significant industry, business, or corporate experience relevant to the energy management industry. The position is full-time, tenure-track starting January 2027 (preferred) or August 2027. Colorado Mesa University (CMU) is a state-funded institution that emphasizes quality teaching and research, having embraced the teacher-scholar model. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester; courses are delivered on-campus, online, and in hybrid format, though our main focus is on in-person learning on a dynamic residential campus. In addition to teaching, scholarship within your discipline is expected along with advising students and service at the school and university level. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. The Program Director/Instructor of Energy Management/Landman provides strategic leadership, administration, instruction, and continuous improvement for Colorado Mesa University's nationally recognized Energy Management/Landman Program in the Davis School of Business. The position directs all aspects of the program, including curriculum development, AAPL accreditation, student recruitment, advising, industry engagement, experiential learning, field tours of energy operations, assessment, and instruction. The Program Director serves as the university's primary liaison to the energy industry, professional organizations, alumni, advisory board members, and community partners to ensure graduates are prepared for careers in the energy sector. The position combines responsibilities typically associated with an academic program director, faculty instructor, academic advisor, recruiter, internship coordinator, and industry relations manager.  Salary: $88,000 - $100,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE:    REQUIRED:   Master’s degree in Business, Energy Management, Petroleum Land Management, Natural Resources, Engineering, Law, or a related field. Significant professional experience in the energy industry. Familiarity or experience working with local, state and federal regulatory agencies College-level teaching or professional training experience. Ability to develop experiential learning opportunities. Demonstrated ability to build industry partnerships.   Strong communication and organizational skills. DESIRED:  PhD, Doctorate, or Juris Doctorate with significant industry experience. Professional Landman (PLM), Registered Professional Landman (RPL), or Certified Professional Landman (CPL) designation preferred (or a significant amount of compliance, regulation, and/or land experience). Experience directing an academic program. Experience maintaining specialized accreditation. Experience with curriculum development and assessment. Demonstrated success in student recruitment and retention. Established professional network within the energy industry. How to Apply:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter describing qualifications and experience as they relate to the specific requirements, responsibilities, and preferences of this position. Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. If transcripts and credentials are foreign this must be submitted in English) Examples of recent course/student evaluations of teaching Include the name, phone number, email address and relationship of at least three professional references who can attest to your ability to perform the job you are applying for.   Professional references should include at least one current or former supervisor.   Professional reference may also include current or former employers, colleagues or other professionals who have first-hand knowledge and can recommend you for employment. Direct Inquiries: Dr. Morgan Bridge, mbridge@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Professor-of-Accounting_JR100652": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: The Davis School of Business at Colorado Mesa University is seeking candidates for the rank of Assistant Professor of Accounting with their primary focus in high-quality instruction and curricular innovation. The position is full-time, tenure-track starting January 2027 (preferred) or August 2027. Colorado Mesa University (CMU) is a state-funded institution that emphasizes quality teaching and research, having embraced the teacher-scholar model. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester; courses are delivered on-campus, online, and in hybrid format, though our main focus is on in-person learning on a dynamic residential campus. Davis School of Business is AACSB accredited and the qualified candidate will be expected to maintain Scholarly Academic status. In addition to teaching, scholarship within your discipline is expected along with advising students and service at the school and university level. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Candidates may come from diverse backgrounds, with a range of experiences, achievements, and leadership roles, either within or outside academia. Candidates should have significant industry, business, or corporate experience relevant to accounting.  As a member of the Davis School of Business, you will be expected to teach four classes per semester in a variety of undergraduate and graduate courses such as Principles of Financial and/or Managerial Accounting, Data Analytics for Accounting, Fraud and Forensic Accounting, and Managerial Accounting (graduate).  Salary: $103,000 - $113,00 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE:    REQUIRED:   A PhD or DBA in Accounting, or a closely related field with at least 18 accounting credit hours at the graduate level and significant work experience in accounting. ABD with a dissertation defense date and completion of all degree requirements on or before August 2027 will be considered. Demonstrated potential for exceptional teaching performance. Commitment to best practices in instruction and student advising/mentoring. Demonstrated dedication to advancing a research agenda and producing scholarly work relevant to accounting Demonstrated potential for active involvement in institutional, community, and/or professional activities. Strong communication and organizational skills. DESIRED:  Experience teaching college-level accounting courses beyond student teaching Certified Public Accountant, CPA Five or more years of accounting/business industry experience is strongly preferred given our hands-on, application-oriented approach in the classroom. How to Apply:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter describing qualifications and experience as they relate to the specific requirements, responsibilities, and preferences of this position. Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. If transcripts and credentials are foreign this must be submitted in English) Teaching statement of no more than two pages, should address teaching interests, examples of classroom techniques, and strategies for effective teaching Examples of recent course/student evaluations of teaching Include the name, phone number, email address and relationship of at least three professional references who can attest to your ability to perform the job you are applying for.   Professional references should include at least one current or former supervisor.   Professional reference may also include current or former employers, colleagues or other professionals who have first-hand knowledge and can recommend you for employment. Direct Inquiries : Dr. Chistine Noel, cnoel@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Professor-of-Economics_JR100653": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: The Davis School of Business at Colorado Mesa University is seeking candidates for the rank of Assistant Professor of Economics with their primary focus in high-quality instruction and curricular innovation. The position is full-time, tenure-track starting January 2027 (preferred) or August 2027. Colorado Mesa University (CMU) is a state-funded institution that emphasizes quality teaching and research, having embraced the teacher-scholar model. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester; courses are delivered on-campus, online, and in hybrid format, though our main focus is on in-person learning on a dynamic residential campus. Davis School of Business is AACSB accredited and the qualified candidate will be expected to maintain Scholarly Academic status. In addition to teaching, scholarship within your discipline is expected along with advising students and service at the school and university level. There may also be potential opportunity to work on technical reports and economic updates. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Candidates may come from diverse backgrounds, with a range of experiences, achievements, and leadership roles, either within or outside academia. Candidates should have significant industry, business, or corporate experience relevant to economics.  As a member of the Davis School of Business, you will be expected to teach four classes per semester in a variety of undergraduate and graduate courses such as Principles of Micro and/or Macro Economics, Intermediate Microeconomic Theory, Managerial Economics (graduate), and Labor Economics. Salary: $92,000 - $98,500 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE:    REQUIRED:   A PhD in Economics, or a closely related field with at least 18 economics credit hours at the graduate level and significant work experience in economics. ABD with a dissertation defense date and completion of all degree requirements on or before August 2027 will be considered. Demonstrated potential for exceptional teaching performance. Commitment to best practices in instruction and student advising/mentoring. Demonstrated dedication to advancing a research agenda and producing scholarly work relevant to economics Demonstrated potential for active involvement in institutional, community, and/or professional activities. Strong communication and organizational skills. DESIRED:  Experience teaching college-level economics courses beyond student teaching Five or more years of economics/business industry experience is strongly preferred given our hands-on, application-oriented approach in the classroom. How to Apply:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter describing qualifications and experience as they relate to the specific requirements, responsibilities, and preferences of this position. Curriculum Vitae (CV) Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. If transcripts and credentials are foreign this must be submitted in English) Teaching statement of no more than two pages, should address teaching interests, examples of classroom techniques, and strategies for effective teaching Examples of recent course/student evaluations of teaching Include the name, phone number, email address and relationship of at least three professional references who can attest to your ability to perform the job you are applying for.   Professional references should include at least one current or former supervisor.   Professional reference may also include current or former employers, colleagues or other professionals who have first-hand knowledge and can recommend you for employment. Direct Inquiries: Dr. Nate Perry, naperry@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Montrose-Campus-Montrose-CO/Instructor-of-Nursing_JR100618-1": {
      "title": "Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking qualified applicants for a non-tenure track Instructor of Nursing to teach in the PN and LPN-BSN nursing programs at Montrose campus. This position has ongoing responsibility for facilitating student learning in the classroom (in-seat and/or via distance education), laboratory, and/or clinical practice setting. The Instructor of Nursing also assumes joint responsibility with faculty in guiding student learning. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Supervise students’ performance of clinical skills in the lab and/or clinical setting. This includes the ability to demonstrate clinical skills as needed for student learning.   Collaborate with nursing faculty and agency contacts to arrange for clinical experiences in local health care facilities.   Demonstrate clinical skills as needed for student learning.   Supervise student performance of clinical skills and patient care.   Evaluate student performance in the clinical setting, including clinical written assignments under the direction and supervision of nursing faculty.   Reinforce theoretical and evidence-based content with nursing examples and clinical expectations.   Develop positive relationships with other faculty, students, and the clinical sites.   Facilitate socialization of students into professional registered nurses.   Teach assigned classes. This includes content preparation with an emphasis on student engagement and adult learning theory.   Incorporate classroom management skills and use of CMU’s learning management system platform required.   Inform all students attending class, in writing and within the time span established by departmental policy, of the course description, policies, and grading criteria.   Establish, post, and maintain a minimum of five office hours weekly during each academic term of the academic year. Office hours may vary in delivery (i.e., Zoom, Teams, mornings, afternoon, evening hours) for in-person, online, and hybrid courses or based upon the courses taught and student availability to meet.   Teach the standard teaching load of 12 credit hours per semester; some assigned courses may be taught face-to-face, online, or hybrid delivery modalities.     Attend monthly faculty meetings and biannual workdays to support program operations, faculty collaboration, and student success.   Assist with and/or proctor simulation activities, examinations, and student orientations scheduled throughout the semester for assigned courses and the Practical Nursing (PN) program.   Willingness to teach across programs offered at the Montrose and Grand Junction campus as needs arise.      SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES   This position reports to the Director of Nursing Education Programs and the Director of Health Sciences and does not currently have supervisory responsibilities over other faculty/staff.   QUALIFICATIONS  To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.     REQUIRED EDUCATION, LICENSURE, and EXPERIENCE   A current license in good standing to practice as a registered nurse in Colorado. A minimum of one year of clinical experience relevant to the area(s) of responsibility with not less than 2 years of full-time (or equivalent) professional nursing practice. Hold a minimum of a graduate degree in nursing from an accredited college or university with national nursing accreditation. If the graduate degree is non-nursing, the individual must have a bachelor’s degree in nursing from an accredited college or university and demonstrate evidence of the graduate degree being in a field relevant to the area of responsibility, OR If an applicant is in a graduate program, they must have a bachelor’s degree in nursing from an accredited college or university and submit a written plan demonstrating ongoing progression in obtaining a graduate degree in nursing or in a field relevant to instructional content within 3 years of hire.   Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Salary: $54,000-$60,00 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! HOW TO APPLY:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries: Dena Banta Corona, dbantacorona@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Clinical-Professor-for-Master-of-Science-in-Occupational-Therapy_JR100562": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor/Clinical Professor for Master of Science in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor for the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy Program with practice mastery in physical rehabilitation. This is a full-time tenure-track or clinical-track, 12-month position with a start date of January 6, 2027. The standard academic load is 18-20 credit hours per year primarily on site; courses may be assigned as in-person or hybrid. Participation in scholarship, advising, and service to the program, department, and profession are expected. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teach graduate-level courses within the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy Program. Develop and coordinate course design, course delivery, and participate in the evaluation of didactic and clinical curriculum. Advise and mentor graduate students, including guiding faculty-led research projects Initiate an ongoing scholarly agenda in area of expertise. Ongoing development and evaluation of curriculum to align with program goals and accreditation standards. Support admissions and applicant screening processes Complete professional development activities and service to the Department, University and community. Participate in ACOTE accreditation, and program/University assessment processes. Perform other program and department level duties as assigned. Salary: $95,000-$100,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty and responsibility satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE:  Minimum Qualifications Required:  EITHER A) Occupational therapist with the following: Master's degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program AND currently pursuing a Doctoral degree, or entry-level Doctoral degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program. Must have certification from the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT). Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Colorado. Minimum of two years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. OR B) Post-professional OTD/DOT degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program. Must have certification from the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT). Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Colorado. Minimum of two years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. All candidates should possess excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Detail-oriented with strong organizational, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities. Ability to work effectively as a member of a team. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical experience in adult physical rehabilitation. Previous academic teaching experience. Clinical teaching experience as a Level II Fieldwork educator. Evidence of scholarship (presentations, articles, posters, etc.). Active in community service and participation Leadership in local, regional, or national occupational therapy associations An earned terminal doctoral degree in an appropriate discipline (PhD, EdD). Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with adults in physical rehabilitation settings, working with students from diverse backgrounds, and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Open until filled.   To ensure consideration, complete applications must be received by September 15, 2026. How to Apply : Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.  Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact: Sarah Gray, search Chair at: sgray2@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Tech-Grand-Junction-CO/Technical-Instructor-of-Medical-Office-Assisting_JR100467": {
      "title": "Technical Instructor of Medical Office Assisting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: We are seeking a passionate and experienced Medical Assistant Instructor to join our faculty. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in medical assisting and a dedication to teaching and mentoring students. As a Medical Assistant Instructor, you will be responsible for delivering high-quality instruction, developing curriculum, and ensuring that students acquire the skills and knowledge necessary to excel in the medical field. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Conduct both lecture and lab instruction for 15 credit hours per semester and maintain 5 hours of office time per week for student consultation and support Work independently and collaboratively with colleagues to develop innovative curriculum that addresses the needs of our diverse student population. Demonstrate extensive knowledge and experience in medical assisting, utilizing the most current equipment and technology to enhance instruction in clinical and administrative procedures. Working knowledge and skill of up-to-date medical assisting principles, methods, and techniques. Evaluate student performance in coursework using industry-related standards and expectations to ensure competency and readiness for the workforce. Determine program needs and manage the program budget, including purchasing and cost control, to maintain high-quality educational resources. Maintain knowledge of industry-standard medical equipment and demonstrate its functionality in instructional settings. Engage successfully with students, healthcare professionals, other educators, and the public in a professional and courteous manner. Assist in the recruitment, advisement, placement, and development of cooperative work experience opportunities for students, and conduct follow-up with graduates. Serve as a representative of the department by participating in committees, task forces, and events at the campus, college, and/or state levels. Exhibit excellent organizational, communication, and presentation skills, along with a positive and enthusiastic attitude towards teaching and student success Excellent organization, communication, and presentation skills. Positive and enthusiastic attitude. Advise students, maintain student files and paperwork, including job sheets, registration, and intent to graduate. Coordinate industry engagement with local employers for advisory committee, internship, and other industry specific needs. Perform all responsibilities and instructional duties in accordance with local, state, and federal regulations as well as CMU Tech/CMU policies and procedures. Ensure the maintenance of appropriate approvals & accreditation, maintain and develop the curriculum in step with industry and state requirements. Promote a positive collegiate atmosphere and develop positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Applicant will perform other duties as required. Salary: $53,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! QUALIFICATIONS: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Minimum Qualifications Required: Minimum of 4,000 hours of w ork experience as a Medical Assistant in a clinical setting within the last five years. Preferred Qualifications: Associate degree or higher in related field Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) or Registered Medical Assistant (RMA) credentials. Evidence of teaching ability and or previous teaching experience in field COMPUTER SKILLS Ability to utilize PowerPoint, Learning Management System technology to maintain grades and content. LANGUAGE SKILLS Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures and governmental regulations.  Ability to write reports, business correspondence and procedure manuals.  Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, clients, customers and the public. MATHEMATICAL SKILLS Ability to apply accounting models and mathematical concepts such as probability and statistical inference.  Ability to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios and proportions to practical situations. REASONING ABILITY Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Ability to interpret an extensive variety of technical instructions in mathematical or diagram form, to interpret an extensive variety of legal and regulatory documents and deal with several abstract and concrete variables. PHYSICAL DEMANDS  The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, walk, sit, and talk or hear.  The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 40 pounds.  Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus. WORK ENVIRONMENT  The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The employee typically performs the duties of the job in an open office setting.  The noise level in the work environment is moderate to loud at times, with several disruptions throughout the day. This position will remain open until filled. Applications received by 9/1 will receive priority consideration, and applications received after that date will be reviewed on a weekly basis until the position is filled. Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Instructor-of-Nursing_JR100108": {
      "title": "Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking a qualified graduate-prepared registered nurse for a non-tenure track Instructor of Nursing to primarily teach in the traditional Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSNt) program in Grand Junction and surrounding communities. This position seeks candidates with at least two years of pediatric and/or obstetrical clinical nursing expertise and includes the role of clinical lead. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. The standard teaching load is 12 course credit hours per semester or 24 credits over an academic year. Teaching theory, laboratory, and/or clinical components (i.e., clinical orientations, labs, clinicals, simulations) in nursing education programs. Willingness to teach across programs (PN, LPN-BSN, AAS, BSNt, MSN/DNP) based on program needs. Primary teaching commitment includes teaching and facilitating the obstetric/pediatric clinical in the BSNt program. Collaborate with various healthcare facilities and secure appropriate clinical placements. Schedule student placements and ensure each student rotation consists of required clinical hours. Supervising student performance of clinical skills simulation, laboratory, and/or patient care in the clinical settings (clinical faculty-to-student ratio is not more than 1:10). This includes the ability to demonstrate clinical skills as needed for student learning. Evaluate student performance in the clinical, simulation, and/or laboratory setting, including grading of clinical written assignments while using CMUs learning management system. Reinforce theoretical and evidence-based content with nursing examples and clinical expectations. Maintaining and promoting positive and productive relationships with healthcare agencies to support high-quality clinical placements. Monitoring and evaluating clinical learning environments to ensure appropriate student learning opportunities. Facilitate socialization of students into the professional registered nurse and/or advanced nurse role. Assist with recruiting and mentoring adjuncts teaching clinicals. Establish, post, and maintain a minimum of five office hours weekly during each academic term of the academic year. Office hours may vary in delivery (i.e., Zoom, Teams, mornings, afternoon, evening hours) for in-person, online, and hybrid courses or based upon the courses taught and student availability to meet. Maintaining clinical expertise. Minimum Qualifications Required: Eligible for or holding a current license in good standing to practice as a Registered Nurse in Colorado.  Minimum of two years of full-time professional clinical obstetric and/or pediatric nursing experience. Graduate degree in nursing from a national accredited school of nursing. Demonstrate knowledge and skills related to: Adult learning principles Teaching methodology Curriculum development and evaluation Or a written plan for obtaining such knowledge beginning no later than the first year of teaching. Salary: $54,000-$60,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! Priority consideration will be given to applications received by June 14, 2026. Applications submitted after this date may be reviewed weekly until the position is filled. How to Apply: Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload the following: Cover letter related to the specific requirements and responsibilities of this position Resume Include the name, phone number, email address and relationship of at least three professional references who can attest to your ability to perform the job you are applying for. Professional references should include at least one current or former supervisor.  Professional reference may also include current or former employers, colleagues or other professionals who have first-hand knowledge and can recommend you for employment. Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact: Lynn Duncan lduncan@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Kinesiology_JR100111": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: CMU encourages students to engage in a healthy campus lifestyle. As part of our campus-wide Health and Wellness program, every student takes the Health & Wellness course and at least one activity class (and most take three or more) to meet graduation requirements for all undergraduate degrees. Our activity classes range from Aerobics to Zumba and we are always looking for local instructors who are highly experienced in the courses we offer. With the great community of health, fitness, and wellness experts we enjoy in Western Colorado, YOU could be a great fit to educate our Mavericks! Please explore the list below to see our full list of course offerings. If you see an activity you are trained in and passionate about, we encourage you to apply and join the Maverick family! List of Activity Courses: Beginning Swimming, Intermediate Swimming, Springboard Diving, Water Polo, Rock Climbing, Hiking, Beginning Golf, Intermediate Golf, Disc Golf and Ultimate Frisbee, Badminton, Karate, Beginning Tennis, Pickleball, Racquet Sports, Fitness Walking, Physical Conditioning, Intermediate Weight Training, Weight Training, Aerobics, Step Aerobics, Self-Defense, Pilates, Indoor Cycling, Adaptive Physical Activity, Introduction to Yoga, Hatha Yoga Relaxation, Flow Yoga, Zumba, Snorkeling/Free Diving, and Social Dance. In addition to our activity classes, we are also looking for instructors who may be interested and qualified to teach the Health & Wellness course. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teaching as an Adjunct Lecturer at CMU requires familiarity and use of our online learning platform, D2L, along with the ability to create a syllabus with engaging and educating methodologies to assess student learning.  Salary: $600-$850 per credit hour. Commensurate with education and experience. ‌ Minimum Qualifications Required: Bachelor’s degree or higher or we will consider accredited certification in your activity and/or 5 years of documented experienced teaching.  Master's degree is required to teach KINE 100 Health and Wellness How to Apply : Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.  Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact:  Kristin Heumann, kheumann@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Lecturer-of-Business_JR100078": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking applications for a part-time in-person Lecturer of Economics. The ideal candidates would have experience teaching Economics principles courses. Part-time faculty at CMU are part-time employees who are hired on an as-needed basis. This job ad is to collect applications for qualified lecturers but communication to applicants may be delayed as faculty needs fluctuate. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. This position will consist of teaching one to two 3-credit hour courses per semester, starting fall 2026 (mid-August). Courses taught will be primarily the 200-level Principles of Microeconomics and/or Principles of Macroeconomics courses the first semester with options to teach upper-level economics courses in the future depending on experience. In addition, the Lecturer must hold a minimum of two office hours weekly for one course, plus a minimum of one office hour for each additional course, up to a maximum of five office hours per week. Salary: $600.00 - $850.00 per credit hour. Adjunct faculty are pair on a per credit hour basis, commensurate with education ad experience. ‌ Minimum Qualifications Required:  Masters degree in Economics or closely-related discipline with at least 18 graduate level credit hours in Economics. Preferred Qualifications: PhD preferred but not required. How to Apply:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a:  Cover letter  Resume  Include the name, phone number, email address and relationship of at least three professional references who can attest to your ability to perform the job you are applying for. Professional references should include at least one current or former supervisor.  Professional reference may also include current or former employers, colleagues or other professionals who have first-hand knowledge and can recommend you for employment.  Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) ​ Direct Inquiries Contact:  Suzanne Owens-Ott; sowens@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    }
